1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,200
What if
every person

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,970
on Earth jumped
at once?

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:05,849
Eight billion
people weigh

4
00:00:05,849 --> 00:00:07,827
five hundred
million tons.

5
00:00:07,827 --> 00:00:11,236
Earth is twelve trillion
times more massive.

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:12,820
Crowded together,

7
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:14,380
we shift Earth
by a fraction

8
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:16,080
of an atom's width.

9
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:18,390
Landing reverses
that recoil.

10
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:20,976
The landing
releases roughly

11
00:00:20,976 --> 00:00:23,671
one point five
trillion joules,

12
00:00:23,671 --> 00:00:26,100
spread across
billions of feet.

13
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:29,160
Knees, shoes, and soil
cushion the impact.

14
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:31,574
A roar and local
vibrations,

15
00:00:31,574 --> 00:00:33,600
not a planet-shattering
quake.

16
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:34,983
But gathering
everyone takes

17
00:00:34,983 --> 00:00:37,103
sixteen hundred
square kilometers,

18
00:00:37,103 --> 00:00:39,043
packed dangerously
tight.

19
00:00:39,043 --> 00:00:41,290
And then everyone
needs to leave.

20
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,220
Water runs short.

21
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:44,400
Roads jam.

22
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,680
Clinics fill.

23
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:47,520
The real crisis
is supporting

24
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:49,510
humanity in
one place.

25
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:51,360
Jump where we live,

26
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:52,420
and pushes
in different

27
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:54,520
directions
partly cancel.

28
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:56,210
Earth barely
notices.

29
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:59,360
Our orbit
stays steady.

30
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:00,680
The bigger
question?

31
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:02,510
How does everyone
get home?
